+# Narrowing the Veterinarian Directory by Specialty
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, on the ground that owner search already demonstrates paged prefix search. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey, so it covered every way of finding a veterinarian without distinguishing between them.
+
+A request arrived to narrow the veterinarian directory to one specialty. Read against the row as written, that request was out of scope, and the row could have been reopened by implication.
+
+The owner decided the row on 2026-08-30.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Hold NG-9 whole.** Decline the narrowing. Rejected: the directory already shows each veterinarian's specialties, so narrowing to one adds no surface a reader has not already seen.
+2. **Retire NG-9.** Open veterinarian search entirely. Rejected: free-text search over veterinarians would repeat what owner search teaches, which is the original reason for the row.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen). Free-text search stays declined; narrowing the directory by an attribute it already displays is in scope.
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 covers free-text search only. Narrowing a listing by an attribute that listing already shows is a separate capability and is in scope.
+
+The narrowing is stated as `REQ-VET-003`, which also records the machine-readable directory as a supported surface. The withdrawn `REQ-VET-002` stays withdrawn and its id is not reused.
+
+The narrowing is named in the request address. No page control is part of this decision; offering one is a later request.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation; the Non-Goals preamble names it decided alongside NG-4 and NG-5.
+- The same reasoning would admit narrowing any listing by an attribute it displays. No such listing is planned.
+- Free-text veterinarian search remains declined, and a request for it proceeds only on a further recorded owner decision.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the capability the narrowing admits.
